      "passage_sha256": "0376c977dfb5ec8c7f5b0075178197627d695fef59ef825c2439582ea8a8f934",
      "ending": "The u-u matrix is hermitian with even identity coefficients on the diagonal. As H is free and has no involutions, subtracting triangular halves of g combinations makes it zero. The symmetrization formula for the framed Wall invariant then gives zero quadratic self-intersections. There are 2k classes in the free rank-2k module from (5.2). Their hyperbolic pairings give a one-sided inverse to their basis matrix. Direct finiteness of matrix rings over ZH (via finite quotients of the free group and finite-dimensional regular representations) makes that matrix invertible. They therefore form a basis of the **whole** middle module.",
